(In thread)  Replied by Tim :    I would assume that (A) 2x is "reasonable" even though balancing the P and N sides (i.e., mobility) requires a ratio of around 3x; the size is reduced as much as practical to keep the cell size down (note that the 0.85um/0.3um is very close to the correct ratio); (B) Keeping all the same size transistors makes it easier to have a consistent layout across all the cells. I didn't design the cells, so the best people to ask are James Stine, Landon Burleson, or Marcus Mellor.

